{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/969076-what-if-helios-moon-and-gaia-lied-from-the-beginning","id":969076,"title":"What if. Helios , Moon and Gaia LIED from the beginning?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-14T00:51:42-07:00","id":969076,"title":"What if. Helios , Moon and Gaia LIED from the beginning?","content":"This: <a href=\"https://cosmosmagazine.com/chemistry/epic-crash-vaporised-baby-earth-and-so-the-moon-was-born\" target=\"_blank\">https://cosmosmagazine.com/chemistry...-moon-was-born</a><br /> <br /> Moon and Helios &quot;sibling&quot; ?<br /> Gaia still silent and never spoke about HIS OWN BODY?! Mhhhhh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T01:33:52-07:00","id":969090,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Gaia is actually a thing in forsaken. Closest to mention I can remember is in Imperial Mysteries for mage where she is a theorized being that apparently eats everyone that comes close to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T04:23:57-07:00","id":969135,"title":"","content":"There have been some half-hints that Gaia might be a thing back in 1e core, but its never come up after. Certainly not in 2e. Helios and Luna, meanwhile, have immediate impact on the game, given the push and pull of Essence their rising and setting have on the Hisil. As well, there are Lunar and Solar spirits, but the closest thing to a Gaia spirit is... well, <i>everything else but the celestial spirits.</i> <br /> <br /> Given the nature of spirits, there's no such thing as siblings in the first place. They're the most powerful spirit that arose from the existance of those celestial objects, not the children of some Milky Way Galaxy spirit parents. At best, they're metaphorically called siblings because of their effects on Earth's Hisil and the flow of essence as well as old Creation mythologies. <br /> <br /> Heck, we don't even know if Helios is the spirit of the sun in the first place. Helios could merely be the largest spirit in charge of the <i>effects</i> of the sun hitting the Earth, and actually only exist around the planet instead of inside the star itself. There's simply too much unknown about these spirit gods to say anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:06:33-07:00","id":969167,"title":"","content":"I always like simple theory from old <b>Book of Spirits</b> - it simple goes that:<br /> <br /> <b>Gaia <i>IS</i> Earth's Hisil</b><br /> <br /> 'Spirit of Mother Earth' is the Earth's own Shadow. It's so vast spirit, Uratha and other spirit's kind are <i>literally walking on her </i>when crossing Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-14-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:36:26-07:00","id":969190,"title":"","content":"Gaia's problem might not be that it's not there, but that it's so damn large and so much everything that it's only feasible response to everything is &quot;This is fine.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:12:51-07:00","id":969204,"title":"","content":"What if, if the Sundering was the BORN of the Moon, instead? And the Pangean were the original &quot;spirit god &quot; scion of Gaia, that loose a part of Itself ?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:40:00-07:00","id":969218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> 