y/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/969076-what-if-helios-moon-and-gaia-lied-from-the-beginning?p=970508#post970508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially related, but I've always thought it would be kinda cool if the Idigam were native to the Mars-sized object that impacted the Earth and scattered the debris that would eventually form the Moon. Maybe Father Wolf wasn't really the one who put the Moon-Banished up there in the first place. Maybe they've been there just as long as Luna has.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhhh MAN there are so many cool ways to spin out a related, similar theory. I wouldn't use yours in my games but good lord is it fun!<br /> <br /> Could be kinda neat to spin it as part of this unending cycle -- once upon a time, the Idigram were tearing it up, got locked inside a prison made of a small celestial body by Alien!Wolf. Eventually, the Idigram escaped for whatever reason, and after completely ruining everything (and killing Alien!Helios/nova-ing the local star) they hopped inside their former prison and hurled themselves out into the stars. . slamming into a young planet, which created the moon that would be their prison, and then later their method of escape. . so on and so forth forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:28:34-07:00","id":971055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbc